  "comments": "<p>Beginning in 1996, series years are denoted by the first letter of a note's serial prefix, while its issuing Federal Reserve Branch is indicated by the second letter.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Solid security thread only visible under a backlight - inscription “USA FIVE” repeated throughout:</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/666bd519bf7c1.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/666bd519bf7c1.jpg\"></a></p><p>© Kiet Tran</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>UV activity at 365nm on a 2001 note:</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6897ba8a223d8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6897ba8a223d8.jpg\"></a> &nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6897ba92608ae.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6897ba92608ae.jpg\"></a></p><p>© Brandon Bertolli</p>",
